>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `Simp`

``` hol4
clasetLib.Simp : thm -> thm
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Marks a theorem as a temporary simplification rule for a clasimp tactic.

`Simp th` is logically equivalent to `th`, but carries a marker recognized
in the theorem-list argument of `AUTO_TAC`, `FORCE_TAC`, `FASTFORCE_TAC`,
`SLOWSIMP_TAC`, `BESTSIMP_TAC`, and `CLARSIMP_TAC`. The enclosed theorem is
added to the invocation simpset and is not inserted as an assumption or
added to the temporary claset.

The marker is temporary. Use the standard `[simp]` declaration mechanism
for a persistent rewrite.

Classical-only and tableau tactics have no simpset and reject `Simp`
instead of silently changing its meaning.

### Failure

Constructing `Simp th` does not validate the rewrite. A consuming clasimp
tactic can fail if the theorem cannot be made into a simplification rule.
Classical-only and tableau tactics reject the marker.

### Example

``` hol4
clasimpLib.AUTO_TAC [clasetLib.Simp my_rewrite]
```

